%N A401420 Triangular numbers t such that either t-1 or t+1 is a perfect power (A001597).
%e A401420 28 is a term because it is a triangular number, and 28-1=27 is a perfect power: 27=3^3.
%t A401420 ppQ[n_] := GCD @@ FactorInteger[n][[;; , 2]] > 1; Select[Accumulate[Range[10^6]], Or @@ ppQ /@ (# + {-1, 1}) &] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 24 2026 *)
